title: Query IR
tags: Query
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: The JSON form every query compiles to — what the daemon receives — one node per predicate or combinator.

A query travels as a recursive JSON object, internally tagged by `type`
(`metafolder_core::query::Query`):

|!Node |!`type` |!Matches |
|IsPresent |`is_present` |the field exists and is not `nothing` |
|IsAbsent |`is_absent` |the field exists and is `nothing` |
|IsUnknown |`is_unknown` |the field does not exist |
|Eq / Neq |`eq` / `neq` |equality, inequality |
|Lt / Lte / Gt / Gte |`lt` / `lte` / `gt` / `gte` |ordered comparison |
|In |`in` |the field equals one of `values` — the `or` of one `eq` per value, same aspect; empty matches nothing |
|And / Or |`and` / `or` |all / at least one of `operands` |
|Not |`not` |`operand` does not match |
|Follows |`follows` |a `ref` or `tree_ref` whose direct referent matches `target` |
|FollowsTransitive |`follows_transitive` |`tree_ref` only: a descendant of `target` (a path, or a sub-query); `inclusive: true` adds the target itself |
|Matches |`matches` |a string field matches a regex `pattern` |
|Osm |`osm` |ordered substrings, `terms` and `mode` (`direct` or `path`) |
|SameAs |`same_as` |shares a value of `field` with a metarecord matching `target` |
|UuidIn |`uuid_in` |the metarecord's uuid is in `uuids` (32 hex; empty matches nothing) |

Every predicate that reads a value — `is_present`, `is_absent`, the comparisons,
`in` and `matches` — takes an optional `aspect` (`value`, `parent`, `path`; omitted for the
default `raw`). `osm` has its own `mode` instead; `is_unknown` reads no component and has none. A
`follows` target is a bare path string or a query object.

```
{"type": "and", "operands": [
  {"type": "gt", "field": "rating", "value": {"type": "int", "value": 3}},
  {"type": "follows_transitive", "field": "mfr_path", "target": "/music/jazz", "inclusive": false}]}
{"type": "osm", "field": "mfr_path", "terms": ["scien", "fic"], "mode": "path"}
{"type": "in", "field": "genre", "values": [{"type": "string", "value": "jazz"}, {"type": "string", "value": "blues"}]}
{"type": "same_as", "field": "mfr_duplicate_group", "target": {"type": "uuid_in", "uuids": ["3f2a…"]}}
```

`uuid_in` is the bridge between the resource layer and the set layer: it lets every
`/query/*` operation target an explicit set — a GUI multi-selection — in one request
rather than one per uuid. The DSL spells it as a bare uuid or `uuid_in(…)`.

`in` is its counterpart over field values: one node where the `or` of its `eq` would
be N + 1, so a long membership list stays clear of the size caps ([[Query limits]]).
It means exactly that `or` — every value is validated as its `eq` would be (no
`nothing`; a `:path` operand is a string), and under `:path` the daemon rewrites it
into that `or` before the forest resolves each path.
